ROI Formula
text

ROI = (Manual Cost - Automation Cost) / Automation Cost * 100

Break-Even Analysis

Break-Even Point: 8 runs (without considering maintenance)

With 20% maintenance overhead, break-even occurs at approximately 10 runs.

Interpretation:

    If the test will be run less than 8 times: Don't automate (negative ROI)

    If the test will be run 8-10 times: Automation breaks even (0% ROI)

    If the test will be run more than 10 times: Automation is profitable (positive ROI)

    ROI increases with each additional run after break-even

Recommendation: Automate the test if it will be executed 10+ times.
